From 8e38f38c2750c56e7197ed240f0802a4b964e86a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 01:13:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] DOS-PORT: patch 0345 -- report when the RTC pump first went
 silent and the first byte went late

The pump's remaining failures on the real 486 are one or a few stuck
repairs and late writes per run (dosags WBH6R: 1 and 1; WBH6W: 1 and 4),
and the status line gives only their totals. SDL 0266 now records the SB
IRQ index of the first of each, and the RTC ticks in the kick interval
before the stuck repair. This puts them on the status line with the song
time they belong to:
- stuck_at=<song_ms>@<loop>/<irq>/<ticks_prev> (in the RTC fragment);
- late_at=<song_ms>@<loop>/<irq>.
Both stay empty when there is no event. With 0275's plan_behind_at= in the
same line, one run on the target then says where each kind of event
fell: in a room load, at a song boundary, or mid-song.

The song ms of an event's slot is back-computed at the first plan that
sees it. The song time planned for a slot is the planner's song clock
minus the slots planned past it, at the measured period. It is exact
between skips, and a plan_behind skip in between shifts it by the skipped
slots. The loop tick is that plan's, within a frame of the event. The
line also gains c_redrain=, the SDL 0265 second register-C reads that
found a flag ('off' when the killswitch is set).

Reporting only: nothing changes when or what the pump writes. The fields
fit the existing buffers (rtc 256, fragment 576, line 768), measured in
the lab.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
